  "raw": {
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7887a8a18473d601a18db7d1533494&lang=en": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix",
      "description": "Position: Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 114-Thrive # of Openings: 1 Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 12-month, grant-funded Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix. Reporting to the Project Director and Director of Student Well-Being, the Project Coordinator is responsible for day-to-day implementation of THRIVE VIA Hendrix, Hendrix College's SAMHSA-funded suicide prevention, mental health, and substance use disorder initiative. Working under the PD, the PC serves as a liaison to the JED Foundation's JED Campus program and leads training logistics, data collection activities, and lethal means assessments. This role requires strong organizational skills; comfort working across academic, clinical, and student affairs stakeholders; and the ability to manage multiple workstreams independently. Working conditions are office environment with some evenings/weekends for trainings and events, occasional in-state travel to community partners, and travel to a required SAMHSA grantee meeting (Washington, DC) with the PD. Key Responsibilities: JED Campus Liaison: Serve as day-to-day point of contact with the JED Campus Advisor and Team; support JED-related assessments; track progress across four program phases. Outreach & Social Media: Collaborate on outreach campaigns and social media content promoting help-seeking and connectedness; track engagement metrics for reporting. Research & Assessment Support: Support an annual needs assessment; maintain records for quarterly and annual reporting. Gatekeeper Training Logistics: Coordinate scheduling, materials, and attendance tracking for GUIDE, MHFA, and QPR trainings. Crisis, Referral, and Lethal Means Coordination: Support community partner agreements and campus-wide 988 promotion; lead environmental scans for access to lethal means. General Program Administration: Support a transition-to-workforce workshop and other project events; assist with budget tracking, match documentation, and grant compliance. Required and Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in psychology, public health, higher education, social work, communications, or a related field; Master’s degree preferred Experience working with college-age students in a health, educational, or nonprofit setting Familiarity with mental health, suicide prevention, or substance use concepts; gatekeeper certification (QPR, MHFA, ASIST) a plus, or willingness to obtain Experience creating and managing social media or digital campaign content Experience with data collection, survey administration, and basic research tasks Strong written and verbal communication skills, adaptable across student, faculty, administrator, and community-partner audiences Demonstrated ability to coordinate across stakeholders and manage multiple workstreams Preferred: Prior experience with a multi-year initiative and federally-funded grant programs Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application and a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. This position is grant funded, contingent on continued federal funding and renewable annually through 9/29/2030. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859e9de070f7019e1cdb2d401a10&lang=en": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Position: Custodian Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-FM-Cust # of Openings: 1 Custodian Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Custodian. Working under the direct supervision of the Custodial Supervisor, the Custodian p rovides routine cleaning of buildings, furniture and equipment on a daily basis and conducts routine housekeeping tasks in accordance with established standards and instruction. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Sweep, mop and scrub floors, stairs (inside and outside buildings) and other surfaces. Must keep all dispensers appropriately filled. Use light and heavy (industrial type) floor machines and attachments. Scrub, strip and wax floors using heavy (industrial type) powered scrubber and buffers. Vacuum rugs/carpets in offices and public areas. Shampoo rugs/carpets periodically using heavy vacuum cleaner and rug shampooing machine. Clean and dust furniture, exhibit cases, pictures, door trim and chalkboards. Clean, equipment and scrubbers and change brushes, pads, rollers, buffers and other attachments. Wash window sills, glass in corridor doors, and clean blinds. Wash and/or clean interior wall s paces while working on ladders. Clean and service lavatories, toilet rooms and restrooms. Collect trash and debris and place in collection area for removal by Facilities personnel. Replace liners in wastebaskets and trash containers. Move heavy furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment, as directed. Submit workorders for needed repairs (doors, door checks, furniture lights, faucets, etc.). Must adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by Facilities Management. Perform a number of special projects related to various aspects of Facilities Management. Complete and/or maintain department records and forms relating to the custodial operation. Conduct routine building inspections to assess needs. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Perform other duties, as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. Ability to bend, stoop, climb ladders, move and/or push/pull equipment. Must be able to lift a minimum of 50 pounds. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must be able to work overtime and/or weekends, when required. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume and contact information for three professional references. Salary is $12.00 per hour. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78879ea15447f701a163dddbb462a7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mover",
      "description": "Position: Mover Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 110-Mover # of Openings: 1 Mover Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Mover. Working under the direct supervision of the Moving Supervisor, the Mover p erforms all aspects of moving requests including set-ups, take-downs, and preparation for special events. Directs the work of Movers or other assigned employees. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform general moving duties and assist other departments when needed. Works closely with requestors and coordinate the movers to ensure adequate coverage for special events in a timely manner. Complete moving/set-up/breakdown work orders and delivery of freight. Operates moving vehicle in conjunction with delivery of freight and performance of moving work order duties. Communicate positively with faculty, staff, and students in completion of duties. Do routine care of all moving vehicles. Deliver housekeeping supplies. Maintains and sets all student room furniture as needed. Assists with all furniture moving on campus. Deliver heavy mail packages and freight deliveries. Maintain a clean and orderly warehouse. Ensure workorders are completed in a timely manner in SchoolDude. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Other duties as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. High School diploma or equivalent. Walking, stooping and climbing for long periods of time. Lifting of objects weighing more than 50 pounds. Ability to withstand extreme hot/cold weather. Operation of heavy equipment. Ability to work safely with hazardous chemicals in a cautious and safe manner. Ability to work overtime and/or weekends. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must have current Arkansas drivers license. The Facilities Department will contact individuals for interviews based on applications submitted through this page. Due to the volume of applications and interest that we receive, we do ask that you refrain from calling our Facilities Department directly. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. . Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7883ac9d02ffb2019d203a127750ca&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Physics",
      "description": "Position: Adjunct Instructor of Physics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-Physics-Adj # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Instructor of Physics The Department of Physics at Hendrix College seeks applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Physics to teach one section of PHYS 160: Astronomy – an introductory survey course intended for non-science majors, for either semester of the 2026-2027 academic year. The instruction of this course takes place on campus and typically meets for three one-hour sessions per week. Instructors are also expected to provide reasonable office hours to support student learning. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. A master’s degree or higher is required. Applications for the position should include a letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae/resume, transcripts (unofficial) from highest degree earned, and list of three references including email address and phone number. Please email any questions to Dr. Julie Gunderson ( gundersonj@hendrix.edu ), Chair of the Physics Department. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where employees treat each other with respect, dignity, and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358052c420ab&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 106-Mgmt # of Openings: 1 Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Hendrix College invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the rank of assistant or associate professor of economics and business specializing in management to begin in August 2027. The successful candidates will work with other Economics and Business faculty to launch a new Business management major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the management field, candidates with interests in sports, healthcare, operations, or supply chain management are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level Business Management courses such as Principles of Management, Organization Behavior, Business Communications, Business Ethics, and upper-level Business Management electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Business Management or a related field such as Business Administration or Business Analytics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and scholarly interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
