    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358b099324bd&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 107-Chem # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of chemistry in the area of pharmaceutical chemistry to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will work with other natural science faculty to launch a new Pharmaceutical Sciences major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. They will teach courses in pharmacology and toxicology, medicinal chemistry, and drug discovery and development and also be expected to contribute to the organic chemistry or biochemistry sequence of courses, depending on their area of expertise. The position comes with competitive start-up funding and carries a full-time teaching load of six course equivalents per year, where one course equivalent comprises a lecture section or two lab sections. Doctorate at time of appointment is required, postdoctoral experience is preferred. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and research interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Chemistry Department Chair Dr. Peter Kett at kett@hendrix.edu , especially if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a13578e7581db4&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 105-Econ # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of economics and business in the area of economics to begin in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the field of economics, candidates with interests in health, environmental, or behavioral economics are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level economics courses such as microeconomics, macroeconomics, statistics, econometrics, economic research, and upper-level economics electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Economics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859fa152cc4201a15f01b2054ea7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Part-Time Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Position: Part-Time Public Safety Officer Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 108-PSO # of Openings: 1 Public Safety Officer (Part-Time) Hendrix College is seeking a part-time, 12-month support staff position. Reporting to the Director of Public Safety, the Public Safety Officer ensures the safety of persons and property on the Hendrix campus and helps manage various emergency situations. The anticipated part-time hours for this position are 8pm to 3:30am, Wednesday-Saturday. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrol campus buildings and grounds to prevent or respond to conduct that is a violation of law and/or College expectations to include incidents of theft, vandalism, fire or fire hazards, disorderly conduct, parking violations, etc. Ensure buildings are locked and unlocked as appropriate. Inspect life safety equipment, which includes checking locks, lighting, fire extinguishers and alarms to confirm they are in working order. Report any public safety incidents and unusual or hazardous conditions on campus to appropriate officials (i.e., inoperative alarms, discharged or defective fire extinguishers, broken windows, etc.). Investigate complaints made by faculty, staff, or students on campus. Investigate traffic accidents on campus. Assist local law enforcement, fire, and other emergency personnel as needed. Foster lasting relationships and trust with students, staff, and faculty through open and effective communication. Provide public safety services such as parking and traffic direction, crowd control, and the like, for special events. Issue parking citations and report traffic violations. Assist police with investigations on campus. Provide visitors directions and general Hendrix College information. Complete all required paperwork on campus incidents and public safety activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Public Safety. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Looking for friendly, motivated, enthusiastic candidates. Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent plus experience in customer service. Knowledge of first aid techniques; CPR certification is a plus. Experience working as a member of a team and building relationships with those you serve and support. In-House training provided. Required Skills: Familiarity with relevant laws; basic knowledge of fire prevention; valid driver’s license; ability to deal effectively with a wide range of individuals, in some instances under stressful, dangerous and/or emergency conditions; ability to handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently; demonstrated integrity; must have the physical ability to perform all job duties. Writing skills that allow for comprehensive reporting of incident response and engagement with members of the College community. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. You can learn more about the College's commitment to diversity and inclusion by reviewing our statement: https://www.hendrix.edu/diversity/statement/. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
